I don't :-).  Wishless is a pain in the neck, if you don't get that 
magic resistance.  So if you play a character who does not have a quest 
artifact that guarantees it, you can easily lose the game at a high 
level.  Moreover, the artifact is an unsafe way of having magic 
resistance...  It seems to me that cloaks of magic resistance are much 
rarer than any other cloak.  (Of course you might polypile one, but that 
takes luck and patience and you may have to survive many dangerous 
situations before you can collect enough magic armour to do so.)

Genocideless on the other hand is not really difficult.  Of the three 
standard classes that are regularly genocided (h,L,;), only mind flayers 
are worth the effort.  It is easy to deal with L using a ring of 
conflict and often this is not even necessary.  ; are harmless with an 
oilskin cloak or an amulet of magical breathing or just by making sure 
you have enough charges in a wand of cold or teleportation (the latter 
does not hold on the plane of water).  For h, you need a ranged weapon 
(wand) and to be careful to teleport them away, if they are created next 
to you.  Moreover, not much is lost, if they succeed to suck a little of 
your knowledge once or twice -- although I agree it is better to avoid 
it :-).

